.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd May 18, 2026
.Dt DTFL_CONFIG_SET_IDLE_MERGE_EFFORT 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_config_set_idle_merge_effort ,
.Nm dtfl_config_idle_merge_effort
.Nd merge work for idle arrangements
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/config.h
.Ft int
.Fn dtfl_config_set_idle_merge_effort "dtfl_config *cfg" "int64_t effort"
.Ft int64_t
.Fn dtfl_config_idle_merge_effort "const dtfl_config *cfg"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A trace merges its batches only as new updates arrive, so an
arrangement whose input goes quiet can be left holding several batches,
and every reader then walks all of them.
.Fn dtfl_config_set_idle_merge_effort
sets the effort that operators maintaining a trace spend when they have
no input to process.
With an
.Fa effort
greater than 0, every operator started by
.Xr dtfl_execute 3
under
.Fa cfg
that keeps a trace (arrange, arrange by key, reduce and the operators
built on it, and arrange from upsert) reschedules itself while its trace
has more than one non-empty batch or a merge in progress.
Each time it runs it does as much merge work as if
.Fa effort
updates had been added to the trace.
Once the trace is a single batch, the operator stops rescheduling
itself.
An
.Fa effort
of 0, the default, turns this off: operators maintain their traces only
when they have updates to process.
.Pp
Larger values compact an idle trace in fewer steps but make each step
longer.
The setting is read when a worker starts, and does not apply to a
worker made with
.Fn dtfl_worker_new_standalone
.Pq Xr dtfl_worker_dataflow 3 .
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_config_idle_merge_effort
returns the current setting.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn dtfl_config_set_idle_merge_effort
returns 0 on success, or
.Er DTFL_EINVAL
if
.Fa cfg
is
.Dv NULL
or
.Fa effort
is negative; the setting is then unchanged.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dtfl_config *cfg = dtfl_config_new();

if (dtfl_config_set_idle_merge_effort(cfg, 1000) != 0)
	errx(1, "%s", dtfl_last_error_detail());
dtfl_execute(cfg, run, ctx, NULL);
dtfl_config_free(cfg);
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_collection_arrange 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_config 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_execute 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_worker_dataflow 3
.Sh HISTORY
These functions are differential dataflow's
.Vt Config::idle_merge_effort
and
.Fn configure ,
which install the same default exertion logic on every trace.
Upstream takes an
.Vt Option<isize> ;
here 0 is
.Dv None ,
and a negative effort, which upstream converts to a very large unsigned
one, is refused.
Upstream also lets a program replace the exertion logic of a single
trace; libdtfl does not expose that.
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
As for
.Xr dtfl_config 3 :
a configuration must not be modified while another thread uses it.
